+## Failure mode exposed (skeptical focus)
+
+`government/daily-sitting.py::bills_without_ballots()` lists every
+`records/bills/*.md` modified in the last 21 days that lacks a `.tsv`, without
+testing bill status. The heuristic cannot tell a live bill from a withdrawn or
+unsponsored document, so it has listed the same three non-eligible files on two
+consecutive sittings (2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18) as though they were pending
+business. A seat that mechanically obeyed "a recorded ballot on each bill above"
+would fabricate ballot artifacts for bills whose sponsors forbade or never
+solicited a vote, and would manufacture a false plenary quorum signal. The
+Clerk's own 2026-11-17 agenda independently records "No bill/ballot before this
+sitting; Clerk will not solicit ballots or fabricate votes." I therefore treat
+the agenda's bill list as a stale label, not an authority to vote.
